DDRL bundles or adapts code and data from the following projects. Each is used
under its own license, reproduced in the linked repositories. Every adapted file
also names its source in its header.

* diffusion_priors (Alexandros Graikos et al., NeurIPS 2022), MIT License.
  https://github.com/AlexGraikos/diffusion_priors
  - prior/unet.py, prior/nn.py, prior/diffusion.py: copied from tsp/ (import
    path changed; prior/diffusion.py adds a missing `import math`).
  - ddrl/prior_init.py (plug_and_play_init): adapted from `runlat` in
    tsp/inference.py.
  - ddrl/latent.py (LatentTourModel, adjacency_from_latent): adapted from
    `InferenceModel` and `normalize` in tsp/inference.py.
  - ddrl/decoding.py (greedy_constrained_tour): starts from the greedy edge
    insertion of tsp/inference.py.
  - ddrl/solver.py (TwoOptSolver): extends `TSP_2opt` in tsp/tsp_utils.py.
  - ddrl/dataset.py (draw_tour, TSPDataset): extend `rasterize_tsp` and
    `TSPDataset` in tsp/tsp_utils.py and tsp/inference.py.
  - The prior checkpoint unet50_64_8.pth is the one distributed by that project.

* OpenAI guided-diffusion / improved-diffusion, MIT License.
  https://github.com/openai/guided-diffusion
  prior/unet.py and prior/nn.py descend from these files through
  diffusion_priors; prior/unet.py also adapts an attention block from OpenAI
  CLIP (https://github.com/openai/CLIP, MIT License).

* DDPO (Kevin Black et al., ICLR 2024), MIT License.
  https://github.com/kvablack/ddpo-pytorch
  - ddrl/sampling.py (ddim_step_with_logprob, sample_trajectory): adapted from
    ddpo_pytorch/diffusers_patch/ddim_with_logprob.py and
    pipeline_with_logprob.py.
  - ddrl/search.py: the sampling / advantage normalization / clipped-ratio
    update loop follows scripts/train.py.

* diffusers (Hugging Face), Apache License 2.0.
  https://github.com/huggingface/diffusers
  The DDIM scheduler (diffusers 0.17.1) is used as a library; the DDIM step in
  ddrl/sampling.py is derived from its DDIMScheduler.step through DDPO.

* DIFUSCO (Zhiqing Sun and Yiming Yang, NeurIPS 2023), MIT License.
  https://github.com/Edward-Sun/DIFUSCO
  - ddrl/cython_merge/cython_merge.pyx: copied unmodified from
    difusco/utils/cython_merge/.
  - ddrl/decoding.py (cython_merge, merge_tour, batched_two_opt_torch): adapted
    from difusco/utils/tsp_utils.py.
  - The DDRL-DIFUSCO variant starts from heatmaps produced by DIFUSCO's released
    checkpoints; see ckpt/README.md.

* learning-tsp (Chaitanya K. Joshi et al.), MIT License.
  https://github.com/chaitjo/learning-tsp
  The city coordinates and Concorde tours of the basic TSP test sets
  (tsp{20,50,100,200}_test_concorde.txt), and the coordinates reused by the
  constrained benchmark files in data/, come from this project.

* Concorde TSP solver (Applegate, Bixby, Chvatal, Cook), academic license.
  The reference tours in data/ were computed with Concorde through pyconcorde
  (https://github.com/jvkersch/pyconcorde) when the benchmark was generated.
